{
  "_comment": [
    "Golden cross-runtime table for zPage language URLs.",
    "",
    "Three surfaces have to agree on one question -- 'what is this variant's",
    "URL, and what is that URL's canonical?' -- and they run in two languages:",
    "",
    "  * the SvelteKit article page, via articleCanonicalHref() /",
    "    articleLanguageAlternates() in src/lib/zpage-language.js,",
    "  * the sitemap, via zpageEntries() in src/lib/server/sitemap.ts,",
    "  * the Django crawler prerender tier, via the port in",
    "    py/dj/apps/g12f/views/crawler.py.",
    "",
    "If they disagree, a search engine sees a sitemap URL whose page declares a",
    "different rel=canonical and discards the entire hreflang cluster. So this",
    "file is the single expected answer, asserted by BOTH suites:",
    "",
    "  ts/svelte/free2z/tests/sitemap-language.test.mjs",
    "  ts/svelte/free2z/tests/text-direction.test.mjs   (the `direction` table)",
    "  py/dj/apps/g12f/test_crawler_language.py",
    "",
    "Change one implementation without the other and both suites fail.",
    "",
    "`available_languages` is exactly what the zPage API reports for a",
    "published page -- real languages sorted by tag, with a non-language source",
    "(the legacy `und` sentinel) kept at the front.",
    "",
    "Every REAL language is advertisable. A variant is skipped only",
    "when its tag names no language at all -- `und`, `mul`, private use. It is",
    "NOT filtered to the four locales the product UI is translated into: an",
    "hreflang needs a valid BCP-47 tag, not a tag we ship a navbar in, and",
    "that filter is why a creator's published `zh-Hans` translation was",
    "advertised nowhere and reachable from nowhere. Script and region stay",
    "exact -- `zh-Hans` is never `zh`, `pt-PT` is never `pt-BR`.",
    "",
    "`sitemap` lists the <loc> values that one published zPage contributes, in",
    "order, each with the xhtml:link cluster attached to it.",
    "",
    "`range` and `normalize` pin the two duplicated ALGORITHMS, not just their",
    "URL output. resolveContentLanguageRange /",
    "_resolve_content_language_range decide which variant a language RANGE",
    "means, and the normalizers decide what a `?lang=` even is. Both exist",
    "twice, in two runtimes, and a divergence lets one URL serve two languages",
    "with contradicting canonicals -- which is what `?lang=cmn` did until the",
    "Python side learned ICU's macrolanguage canonicalization.",
    "",
    "The script comparison is the LIKELY script (CLDR likely-subtags), not a",
    "spelled-out subtag: `zh-TW` and `zh-CN` name no script and are the",
    "commonest hand-written Chinese tags, so a guard reading only an explicit",
    "subtag served a Taiwanese reader Simplified text with no disclosure.",
    "`Intl.Locale.maximize()` and `langcodes.Language.maximize()` agree on",
    "every tag reachable here; these cases are what holds them together.",
    "",
    "Bare `yue` normalizes to `yue-Hant` in BOTH runtimes: Cantonese",
    "is a language, not a script variant of `zh`, and written Cantonese is",
    "overwhelmingly traditional. Bare `zh` deliberately does NOT get the same",
    "treatment and stays `zh` -- see the module docstring in",
    "`py/f2z/languages.py`. Both are pinned above because a default applied in",
    "one runtime and not the other is exactly the one-URL-two-languages bug",
    "this file exists to stop.",
    "",
    "`direction` pins the third duplicated algorithm: which WAY a",
    "variant's text runs. contentDirectionAttribute (JS) and",
    "languages.direction_attribute (Python) are the two implementations, and",
    "this tier renders the same URL as SvelteKit, so a divergence lays one",
    "article out two different ways depending on which upstream answered.",
    "",
    "It pins the ANSWER, not the intermediate script, on purpose: ICU and",
    "langcodes are free to disagree about `ur` being `Arab` or `Aran` -- both",
    "are right-to-left -- and pinning the script would fail on a difference",
    "that changes no layout. A tag that names no language is `auto`, never",
    "`ltr`: 'unknown' and 'left-to-right' are different declarations, and the",
    "browser reading the text itself beats guessing.",
    "",
    "`normalize_runtime_divergence` is the honest residue: tags that are",
    "well-formed BCP-47 but absent from the IANA registry. The JS tier",
    "forwards them, the API answers 400, and both tiers then render",
    "DEFAULT_LOCALE -- so the rendered answer still agrees. Each suite asserts",
    "its own column, and neither may grow a case where the two tiers would",
    "render different CONTENT."
  ],
